# What GitHub counts as this repository's languages.
#
# Only genuinely third-party code is vendored. The test suites and the benchmark
# harnesses under tests/ and benchmarks/ used to be marked vendored too, which was
# wrong on the facts (every file there carries this project's own copyright) and
# wrong in effect: it removed far more C++ than Python, so the language bar reported
# a Qt framework as a Python project.

tools/docs-hooks/doxygen-awesome/** linguist-vendored

# The documentation site: its Markdown, its theme overrides, its CSS and its build
# hooks are the site, not the framework.
docs/**                 linguist-documentation
overrides/**            linguist-documentation
deploy/get.synqt.org/** linguist-documentation
tools/docs-hooks/**     linguist-documentation
tools/pygments-synqt/** linguist-documentation

# A bare .h is ambiguous to GitHub (C, C++ or Objective-C, decided by heuristic on
# the contents). Every header here is C++, so say so rather than let the answer
# depend on which files happen to name a class.
*.h linguist-language=C++
